<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy">
  <p>Last updated: {updated}</p>
  <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how Lazarov &amp; Co Ltd. collects, uses, stores, and protects personal data when you visit this website, contact us, or use forms provided on the website.</p>
  <p>This policy applies to https://lazarovco.com. Product-specific websites, applications, payment providers, app stores, or third-party services may have separate privacy policies.</p>
  <h2>2. Data controller</h2>
  <p>The data controller is Lazarov &amp; Co Ltd., registered at Pliska str. 67, Dupnitsa, 2600, Bulgaria. Company registration number / UIC / EIK: 205550822. Email: nikola@lazarovco.com.</p>
  <h2>3. Personal data we collect</h2>
  <p>Contact form data may include name, email address, subject, message content, product or platform information, and any other information you choose to include.</p>
  <p>When you visit the website, basic technical information may be processed by our hosting provider, including IP address, browser type, device information, request time, pages requested, and server logs needed for security and reliability.</p>
  <p>We use GoatCounter to count visits and understand general website usage. GoatCounter is selected because it is lightweight and privacy-friendly, and it does not rely on cookie-based analytics.</p>
  <h2>4. Why we process personal data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Respond to contact form submissions.</li>
    <li>Provide product support.</li>
    <li>Handle business inquiries.</li>
    <li>Maintain website security and reliability.</li>
    <li>Improve website and product communication.</li>
    <li>Comply with legal obligations.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>5. Legal bases for processing</h2>
  <p>Depending on the situation, we process personal data based on your consent, our legitimate interest in operating and securing the website, the need to respond to your request, or compliance with legal obligations.</p>
  <h2>6. How long we keep personal data</h2>
  <p>We keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described in this policy. Contact form messages may be retained for as long as needed to respond, provide support, keep business records, or handle legal claims.</p>
  <h2>7. Who receives personal data</h2>
  <p>Personal data may be processed by providers that help us operate the website and respond to inquiries, including hosting, email, contact form processing, analytics, legal, accounting, or compliance providers where necessary. We do not sell personal data.</p>
  <h2>8. International transfers</h2>
  <p>Some providers may process data outside the European Economic Area. Where this happens, we rely on appropriate safeguards required by applicable data protection law.</p>
  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>Subject to applicable law, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, object to processing, request data portability, withdraw consent, or lodge a complaint with a data protection authority. To exercise your rights, contact nikola@lazarovco.com.</p>
  <h2>10. Security</h2>
  <p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect personal data. However, no website or internet transmission is completely secure.</p>
  <h2>11. Children</h2>
  <p>This website is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children through this website.</p>
  <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. The latest version will be published on this page with an updated date.</p>
</LegalLayout>
